umiproc patch 0011: an IMU initialisation does not set Tracking to OK after Tracking started another map

What: LocalMapping::InitializeIMU remembers the atlas's current map when it starts, and at its end sets
Tracking::mState = OK only if that is still the current map.
Why: InitializeIMU runs in LocalMapping and takes seconds for VIBA 1 and 2 (FullInertialBA, 100 iterations). If
tracking is lost meanwhile and Tracking starts a new map (CreateMapInAtlas: state NO_IMAGES_YET, no reference or
last keyframe, mbVelocity false), the unconditional `mpTracker->mState=Tracking::OK` at the end put Tracking into
the tracking branch for a map that has no keyframe: Track -> TrackReferenceKeyFrame (new map not IMU-initialised,
no velocity) -> ORBmatcher::SearchByBoW(mpReferenceKF = NULL) -> KeyFrame::GetMapPointMatches locks mMutexFeatures
of a NULL keyframe (offset 0x1150 in this build). Upstream ORB-SLAM3 v1.0 has the same line.
Evidence: on the regenerated input of episode 000128, under gdb: "start VIBA 2", tracking lost, "Creation of new map
with id: 1", "end VIBA 2", then SIGSEGV in the main (Tracking) thread in pthread_mutex_lock(mutex=0x1150).
Behaviour change: only when Tracking started another map during an IMU initialisation: Tracking keeps its own state
(it initialises the new map as usual). Not changed: the rest of that InitializeIMU still works on
mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap() (the fork's and upstream's code), which after such a switch is the new map.

diff --git a/src/LocalMapping.cc b/src/LocalMapping.cc
index fd48367..451bcfe 100644
--- a/src/LocalMapping.cc
+++ b/src/LocalMapping.cc
@@ -1121,6 +1121,8 @@ void LocalMapping::InitializeIMU(float priorG, float priorA, bool bFIBA)
     if (mbResetRequested)
         return;
 
+    Map* pMapInit = mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap();   // umiproc patch 0011: the map this initialisation works on
+
     float minTime;
     int nMinKF;
     if (mbMonocular)
@@ -1364,7 +1366,11 @@ void LocalMapping::InitializeIMU(float priorG, float priorA, bool bFIBA)
     }
     mlNewKeyFrames.clear();
 
-    mpTracker->mState=Tracking::OK;
+    // umiproc patch 0011: only while Tracking is still on the map just initialised. If it started a new map during
+    // the initialisation (VIBA 2's FullInertialBA takes seconds), forcing OK made it track the new, empty map with no
+    // reference keyframe (TrackReferenceKeyFrame -> SearchByBoW(NULL) segfaulted).
+    if (mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap() == pMapInit)
+        mpTracker->mState=Tracking::OK;
     bInitializing = false;
 
     mpCurrentKeyFrame->GetMap()->IncreaseChangeIndex();
